          "elapsed_ms": 4523.190667001472,
          "answer": "Division asks how many times one number fits into another. For example, \\(6 \\div 2 = 3\\) because \\(2 \\times 3 = 6\\). So \\(6 \\div 0\\) would need a number that, multiplied by zero, equals six. But zero times any number is zero, never six. Thus no quotient works when the dividend is nonzero. For \\(0 \\div 0\\), every number multiplied by zero gives zero. That means there is no unique quotient for \\(0 \\div 0\\). Therefore, division by zero is undefined.",
